187 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 124 0 R
/E (The Business Responsibility and Sustainability Reporting \(BRSR\) framework has significantly expanded the availability of non-financial data for Indian listed companies. However, the presence of disclosure alone does not ensure meaningful understanding of sustainability performance. In practice, BRSR reports are often read as compliance documents, with limited effort made to interpret the data comparatively or to assess performance outcomes across firms.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
188 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 124 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [3 4]
>>
endobj
189 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 124 0 R
/E (The analysis reveals that while all firms demonstrate compliance with BRSR requirements, sustainability performance varies considerably across both environmental and social dimensions. Improvements in greenhouse gas emission intensity are visible across the sector; however, the pace and consistency of )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
190 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 124 0 R
/E (improvement differ markedly between firms. Higher renewable energy adoption does not necessarily uniformly translate into lower emission intensity, indicating that operational efficiency and process-level interventions remain critical drivers of environmental outcomes.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
191 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 124 0 R
/E (On the social dimension, workforce safety, employee well-being expenditure, and gender-related indicators exhibit uneven performance and slower progress relative to environmental efficiency metrics. The integrated ESG assessment highlights imbalances in sustainability strategies, with firms often performing strongly in one dimension while lagging in others.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
192 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 124 0 R
/E (Overall, the findings suggest that sustainability efforts within the automobile sector remain fragmented, and that BRSR disclosures, when analyzed systematically, can provide insights that go beyond descriptive reporting. The report argues for a shift towards outcome-focused interpretation of BRSR data and highlights areas where firms can strengthen the integration of environmental efficiency and social performance to improve long-term resilience.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
