/T (Across all companies, a downward trend in emission intensity is observed, indicating gradual improvements in carbon efficiency over the study period. However, the rate and consistency of improvement vary considerably. Tata Motors demonstrates the most pronounced and sustained decline, suggesting effective efficiency measures and operational improvements. Ashok Leyland also shows steady improvement, though from a higher initial intensity level. Mahindra & Mahindra and Maruti Suzuki exhibit more modest reductions, with periods of stagnation visible in the trend lines. These patterns suggest that while sector-wide improvements are occurring, the depth and effectiveness of decarbonisation efforts differ substantially across firms.)
