/T (Social performance within the automobile manufacturing sector is closely linked to operational risk, workforce stability, and long-term productivity. Unlike environmental indicators, which often show gradual improvement through efficiency gains, social indicators tend to reflect deeper structural conditions related to labour practices, safety culture, and human capital investment. This section analyses workforce-related social performance using indicators drawn from BRSR disclosures, with a focus on occupational safety, employee well-being expenditure, and gender-related outcomes.)
/E (Social performance within the automobile manufacturing sector is closely linked to operational risk, workforce stability, and long-term productivity. Unlike environmental indicators, which often show gradual improvement through efficiency gains, social indicators tend to reflect deeper structural conditions related to labour practices, safety culture, and human capital investment. This section analyses workforce-related social performance using indicators drawn from BRSR disclosures, with a focus on occupational safety, employee well-being expenditure, and gender-related outcomes.)
