/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 136 0 R
/T (Lost Time Injury Frequency Rate \(LTIFR\) is one of the most outcome-oriented social indicators available within the BRSR framework. It directly reflects workplace safety conditions and is particularly relevant in manufacturing contexts where physical risk exposure is high. The comparative analysis indicates meaningful variation in LTIFR outcomes across firms. While some companies demonstrate relatively strong safety performance, others continue to record higher injury rates, signalling persistent safety risks. These differences are significant because LTIFR outcomes are not solely determined by disclosure practices, but by operational discipline, safety culture, and the extent to which safety standards are enforced across both permanent and contractual workforce segments.)
/E (Lost Time Injury Frequency Rate \(LTIFR\) is one of the most outcome-oriented social indicators available within the BRSR framework. It directly reflects workplace safety conditions and is particularly relevant in manufacturing contexts where physical risk exposure is high. The comparative analysis indicates meaningful variation in LTIFR outcomes across firms. While some companies demonstrate relatively strong safety performance, others continue to record higher injury rates, signalling persistent safety risks. These differences are significant because LTIFR outcomes are not solely determined by disclosure practices, but by operational discipline, safety culture, and the extent to which safety standards are enforced across both permanent and contractual workforce segments.)
