<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 141 0 R
/T (Social performance indicators, particularly LTIFR and well-being expenditure, reveal persistent workforce-related risks within the sector. Given the labour-intensive and high-risk nature of automobile manufacturing, workforce safety should be treated as a core operational risk rather than as a peripheral social responsibility issue. Industry-level initiatives could focus on harmonising safety standards across permanent and contractual workforce segments and encouraging firms to link safety outcomes with management accountability. )
/E (Social performance indicators, particularly LTIFR and well-being expenditure, reveal persistent workforce-related risks within the sector. Given the labour-intensive and high-risk nature of automobile manufacturing, workforce safety should be treated as a core operational risk rather than as a peripheral social responsibility issue. Industry-level initiatives could focus on harmonising safety standards across permanent and contractual workforce segments and encouraging firms to link safety outcomes with management accountability. )
